// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_lnx_pnscan_binary_cli_pattern.yml
// ID Sigma: 97de11cd-4b67-4abf-9a8b-1020e670aa9e
// Título: Pnscan Binary Data Transmission Activity
// Descripción: Detects command line patterns associated with the use of Pnscan for sending and receiving binary data across the network.
This behavior has been identified in a Linux malware campaign targeting Docker, Apache Hadoop, Redis, and Confluence and was previously used by the threat actor known as TeamTNT

// Fecha de creación: 2024-04-16
// Fecha de modificación: 
// Aplica a: Producto: linux | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: linux
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\linux\process_creation\proc_creation_lnx_pnscan_binary_cli_pattern.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine matches regex "-(W|R)\\s?(\\s|\"|')([0-9a-fA-F]{2}\\s?){2,20}(\\s|\"|')"
